StrongAuth ChangeLog

1.0.1 — 2026-09-21
  Login-flow fixes (passkey-enrollment regression)
  * FIXED: enrolling a Passkey silently flipped internal-domain users from
    pass_through to factor_choice — the next M365/SSO login (which posts no
    factor) was bounced back to the login page by afterLogin's "no factor
    presented" check. Step-up on top of the IdP MFA is now opt-in via
    STRONGAUTH_REQUIRE_2FA_IDP only (Orchestrator internal branch).
  * FIXED: any login authenticated via strongauth_sso now passes the factor
    gate (the IdP's own MFA is the second factor) regardless of the user's
    internal/local classification — previously a passkey/TOTP holder or a
    mis-classified email could be double-gated on an SSO login
    (actions_strongauth afterLogin).
  * Admin branch restored to "enrolled factors are honored" semantics (my
    interim pass_through-always was reverted); break-glass still exempts
    admins from the IdP-only rule, and SSO logins pass via the rule above.
  * Login page: the 6-digit box renders only when the pending path offers
    TOTP; passkey-only users now see a "continue with Passkey" hint instead
    of a code box they have no secret for. The same box accepts a backup
    code (lost-authenticator recovery — previously backup codes had no
    entry point on the login page).
  * Passkey management: per-credential list with delete on the manage page
    ( StrongAuth_WebauthnRepo::deleteCredential, audit-logged).
  * Diagnostics: STRONGAUTH_CODE_REV marker (shown in setup ▸ Maintenance)
    + temporary htdocs/check_sso.php probe (code rev, module file mtimes,
    OPcache status/invalidate, resolved auth path, constants, audit tail,
    SSO session tail) — to be deleted after deployment is verified.

1.0.0 — 2026-09-17
  Core authentication
  * RFC 6238 TOTP second factor (6 digits / 30s / SHA-256 / ±1 step, hard-coded)
  * AES-256-GCM encryption of TOTP secrets (v1:iv:tag:ct format, entity-0 master key)
  * Backup codes: bcrypt-hashed, single-use, count configurable (1–50)
  * Optional WebAuthn/FIDO2 Passkey — internal-domain users only, enforced at
    registration UI, JSON endpoint, and login verification (3 layers)
  * Account lockout: GLOBAL per user (cross-entity) after N failures, admin-configurable
  * 30-day device-trust cookies with UA fingerprint + auto-revoke on mismatch (off by default)

  Single sign-on
  * OIDC providers: Entra ID (M365), Google Workspace, self-hosted/generic OIDC
    (Apple sign-in removed by policy — SSO restricted to corporate directories;
    Apple users still get Passkey via iCloud Keychain as a second factor)
  * Authorization Code + PKCE (S256), state/nonce, 10-min challenge TTL, single-use
  * ID-token verification: signature (JWKS), iss, aud, nonce; email_verified=false rejected
  * Google: optional hosted-domain (hd) pinning via tenant_id field
  * Entra: dedicated-tenant guidance (save warns on common/consumers/organizations)
  * Apple: REMOVED — personal-identity emails widen the bypass surface; Passkey
    (iCloud Keychain) remains available to Apple-device users as a factor
  * SSO pickup via Dolibarr native pipeline: module_parts['login'] +
    check_user_password_strongauth_sso() one-time cookie; works alongside local passwords
  * Email is the identity link; optional auto-provisioning with disabled- placeholder
    (no local password possible)

  Login-flow integration (Dolibarr 22/23/24)
  * afterLogin hook: factor policy, lockout, device trust, forced enrollment,
    internal-domain password rejection (IdP-only by design)
  * Correct pending-2FA mechanics: rollback + session_reset before marker writes
    (prevents the dol_login session-resume bypass)
  * Login page: 6-digit input, Passkey button + ceremony JS, trust-device checkbox,
    SSO provider buttons, username prefill, policy-rejection banners

  Admin & audit
  * Permissions: strongauth->reset (manage others / IdP config / key rotation /
    migration), strongauth->audit (log viewer)
  * Setup page with deployment self-checks: composer deps, authentication method,
    multicompany entity coverage, internal-domains-without-IdP
  * IdP configuration with encrypted client secrets and Apple private keys
  * Append-only audit log (11 event types) → SIEM; entity-scoped viewer
  * AES key rotation with transactional re-encryption
  * Optional one-shot totp2fa migration (AES-CBC legacy decrypt → AES-256-GCM),
    explicit and independent of the totp2fa module

  Fixes applied during the 2026-09-17 security audit
  * Removed 2FA bypass via missing/ordered session_reset in login abort helpers
  * Fixed entity context: $conf->entity everywhere (Dolibarr has no $db->entity)
  * Unified bootstrap (lib/strongauth.lib.php) — module classes were never autoloadable
  * SSO endpoints reachable pre-login (NOLOGIN); replaced dead beforeLogin hook
  * Locked down json.php: internal-domain + master-switch checks on registration,
    available_factors check on assertion start
  * Wired STRONGAUTH_REQUIRE_2FA_LOCAL / _IDP to real strategy decisions
  * audit_log user JOIN restricted to current entity; XSS escapes; CSRF checks on
    all admin/view POSTs; descriptor entity handling fixed

  Fixes surfaced by the offline dry-run harness (portable PHP + stubs)
  * Provider_OIDCBase (abstract base) was missing from the bootstrap — every
    provider subclass load would have fatalled
  * isInternalDomain() now lowercases the address (mixed-case emails in
    llx_user were misclassified as external)
  * RobThree 2.x API adaptation: algorithm must be the Algorithm enum (string
    caused TypeError); createSecret takes BITS not chars (20 → 4-char weak
    secret; now 160 bits = 32 chars); provisioning URI assembled in-module
    (getQRCodeUrl removed upstream)
  * QR rendering rebuilt on Dolibarr's bundled TCPDF 2D-barcode encoder —
    fully offline, no external QR API, no totp2fa dependency (needs ext-gd)

  Dry-run coverage: 34-file syntax check, 43 logic assertions (crypto
  roundtrip/tamper, orchestrator policy matrix, lockout state machine, audit
  insert, lang parity, bootstrap wiring), full class-load smoke, and a real
  RFC 6238 end-to-end (live code accept/reject, ±1 window tolerance,
  TCPDF QR PNG pipeline).

  Self-contained packaging (2026-09-18)
  * vendor/ is now bundled with the module (37 MB, pure PHP) — no composer
    step on the server; composer.json kept for dependency refreshes only
  * Dependencies corrected & pinned: firebase/php-jwt ^7 (6.x has open
    security advisories), web-auth/webauthn-framework ~4.0.0 (package name
    fixed — the old "spomky-labs/*" name does not exist on packagist)
  * Factor_WebAuthn rewritten for the real webauthn-framework 4.x API
    (PublicKeyCredentialLoader + Attestation/Assertion validators +
    StrongAuth_WebauthnRepo implementing PublicKeyCredentialSourceRepository;
    the previously-assumed "Server" facade never existed in 4.x); credentials
    stored losslessly as source_json
  * Setup page: one-click "enable SSO authentication method" — rewrites
    conf/conf.php with a timestamped backup (the auth method is a file
    setting, not a database constant)
  * Vendor integration verified offline: 23 assertions covering class
    presence, creation/request options shape, malformed-attestation
    rejection, JWT-v7 JWKS roundtrip + tamper, and live TOTP codes
  * Platform fix: dependencies re-resolved with composer platform.php=8.1
    (symfony pinned to 6.4) — the bundled vendor previously demanded PHP >=8.2
    and broke PHP 8.1 servers; verified on a real PHP 8.1.34 runtime
  * ADMIN BREAK-GLASS: Dolibarr admins are exempt from policy lock-outs —
    an internal-domain admin whose IdP is not yet configured could be locked
    out entirely (password login refused, SSO unavailable). Admins now always
    authenticate with the local password, are never forced into enrollment,
    and still verify enrolled factors when present

  Production rollout fixes (2026-09-18, live debugging on the d-test host)
  * Auto-created tables on enable: deployment-independent fallback (conf.php
    often omits the custom document root, which silently broke the standard
    SQL loader); setup-page one-click schema repair with per-table feedback
  * getLoginPageOptions SSO buttons now vendor-branded: "Microsoft 365" +
    fa-microsoft icon, "Google" + fa-google; friendlier rejection message
  * ProviderRegistry: SELECT missed the `enabled` column — every provider was
    filtered out of the login page regardless of status (test button worked
    because it reads the row directly)
  * OIDC redirect_uri is now absolute (scheme + host) — Azure rejects relative
    URIs with AADSTS90102
  * firebase/php-jwt v7 JWKS adaptation: normalizeJwks() infers alg from kty
    (the original fix used a `?? ` expression inside foreach-by-reference —
    writes went to a temporary copy and never reached the real array)
  * SSO callback redirect carries the CSRF token (required when conf.php
    defines CSRFCHECK_WITH_TOKEN)
  * Admin break-glass made switchable (STRONGAUTH_ADMIN_BREAKGLASS, default
    ON) so internal-domain policy can be enforced for admins too
  * idp_setup rewritten as a provider wizard: vendor cards, guided app
    registration with copy-ready redirect URI, only the 3 required fields;
    new providers default to enabled
  * totp2fa migration tooling REMOVED (scripts/, admin page, lang keys) —
    production never migrated data, totp2fa was disabled instead; users
    enroll fresh through the forced first-login wizard
  * README gains an admin runbook (emergency SQL keys, conf.php auth-method
    setting, break-glass semantics, key-backup warning)

